<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31294" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏvĭŏdūnum</span></b> ,
		i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of several cities in Gaul.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of the Bituriges</i>, near the mod. <i>Nouan</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				7, 12, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 55</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city of the Æduans, on the Loire</i>,
			the mod. <i>Nevers</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				7, 55, 1</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A city of the Suessones</i>, the mod. <i>Soissons</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				2, 12, 1</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
